## Attach step-specific failed step logs to error reasons

### Summary
This PR enhances error reporting by attaching relevant log entries to template build error reasons, providing better debugging information when build step fails.

### Example
```
{
   "reason":{
      "logEntries":[
         {
            "level":"error",
            "message":"[builder 1/1] [stderr]: rm: cannot remove '/gfdsgdagdfg': No such file or directory",
            "timestamp":"2025-09-17T13:00:10.738496303Z"
         },
         {
            "level":"error",
            "message":"[builder 1/1] [stderr]: exit status 1",
            "timestamp":"2025-09-17T13:00:10.738703012Z"
         },
         {
            "level":"error",
            "message":"Build failed: error building step 1: failed to run command `rm /gfdsgdagdfg`: exit status 1",
            "timestamp":"2025-09-17T13:00:11.000753879Z"
         }
      ],
      "message":"failed to run command `rm /gfdsgdagdfg`: exit status 1",
      "step":"1"
   }
}
```

