## What
- replace the stubbed event bus shim with an in-proc priority queue implementation that exposes emit/on/stats/dlq/reset
- keep legacy helpers (publish/subscribe/_peek/DLQ) and surface aliases so eventBus, eventBusV2 and events/priorityBus all point to the same instance

## Why
- addresses gap #2 by standardising on eventBusV2 so debug routes and feature flows receive a working priority bus with DLQ stats

## Files touched
- src/core/eventBusV2.ts

## Risk
- Medium – core event pipeline but legacy API surface maintained

## Testing steps
- `npm test`
- `NODE_PATH=backend/node_modules node -r ts-node/register -e "const mod = require('./src/core/eventBusV2'); console.log(mod.bus.emit && mod.bus.on && mod.bus.stats ? 'ok' : 'missing');"`
- `rg "class PriorityBus" src | grep -v _legacy`
- `npm run typecheck --prefix backend` *(fails: existing missing type definitions – pre-existing)*

